{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/934465-can-nightmares-work-on-ephemeral-beings","id":934465,"title":"Can Nightmares work on Ephemeral Beings?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-20T06:58:47-07:00","id":934465,"title":"Can Nightmares work on Ephemeral Beings?","content":"Title says all the above. <br /> <br /> Last night, one of the players wanted to see if he can try to use his nightmare on a ghost and I wasn't sure the ruling for it. I was curious to get some other opinions. What do you guys think - would it be okay or nah? I'd like to hear you reasons why as well if you can.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11457-volke","name":"Volke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11457_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T07:11:25-07:00","id":934471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Volke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/934465-can-nightmares-work-on-ephemeral-beings#post934465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Title says all the above. <br /> <br /> Last night, one of the players wanted to see if he can try to use his nightmare on a ghost and I wasn't sure the ruling for it. I was curious to get some other opinions. What do you guys think - would it be okay or nah? I'd like to hear you reasons why as well if you can.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I would say that it would work on a ghost or a goetic. Angels and spirits would be immune, as neither were ever human or are connected to the human subconscious, as ghosts were and goetics are, respectively. That's just my opinion though. Perhaps levy a penalty to the activation roll, as a ghost has forgotten many of the human fears that it once possessed? Perhaps the penalty could be based on Rank?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T07:42:21-07:00","id":934489,"title":"","content":"Personally, I would say Nightmares work on most beings, even those that are inherently inhuman, because what Nightmares are in the end is forcing a concept from the Astral on a victim, making it real for them. Arguably, it shouldn't work if you don't understand the emotions (primarily fear) that Nightmares are based on in a close to human way, but if you have a mind or consciousness that can comprehend the idea, then I don't see a very compelling reason for that interpretation.<br /> <br /> It don't think Nightmares ought to necessarily rely on being connected to the soul of humanity to have a comprehensible effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 07-20-2016, 10:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T07:51:36-07:00","id":934494,"title":"","content":"Of course they do.<br /> <br /> Beast the Primordial p133, 'Nightmares function on supernatural creatures just as they do on normal human beings. Even creatures that don\u2019t dream or feel fear can tremble before the power of the Dark Mother. Such beings are, however, better able to resist than human beings.''","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T11:52:20-07:00","id":934628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/934465-can-nightmares-work-on-ephemeral-beings?p=934494#post934494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course they do.<br /> <br /> Beast the Primordial p133, 'Nightmares function on supernatural creatures just as they do on normal human beings. Even creatures that don\u2019t dream or feel fear can tremble before the power of the Dark Mother. Such beings are, however, better able to resist than human beings.''</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I see well I remember reading this but I wasn't sure about the interpretation. Because it also says to be able to use a nightmare:<br /> <br /> Calling forth a Nightmare is a simple endeavor: the Beast<br /> simply touches her victim or meets her gaze and speaks a few<br /> words to trigger the ancient, buried fear that lurks in his soul.<br /> Nightmares require a Beast to make eye contact with her victims in order to invoke their effects. That contact is oneway<br /> \u2014 the victim needs to see the Beast\u2019s eyes, but not vice versa. This contact is possible through simple barriers like<br /> sunglasses (even mirrored) or tinted windows, but does not work when looking at a video feed rather than the Beast<br /> herself.<br /> <br /> So I wasn't sure as you can't technically touch a spirit unless they manifest or some way that makes them physical. <br /> <br /> Thanks for your thoughts on this everyone so far <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11457-volke","name":"Volke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11457_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T14:30:18-07:00","id":934710,"title":"","content":"Eye contact is needed, and it's possible for some ephemerals to not have eyes. But the eye contact only needs to be one way, so if it has eyes and is viewing you in Twilight Form it's still affected. They don't need to manifest if you are in their world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}